hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"73","On voluntary prayer. Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays two rak'ahs after Maghrib before speaking, they are written - or raised - for him in Illiyyun."
"74","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, the nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle; Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed me that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord descends in the last part of the night, and a caller calls out in the highest heaven: Has not the Creator descended? So the inhabitants of heaven prostrate, and a caller calls out among them to that effect, passing no inhabitants of a heaven but that they are in prostration. Abu Dawud said: Sufyan - meaning al-Thawri - used to dislike imagining the modality of this hadith and the like."
"75","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Nasr narrated to us. He said: I asked Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, saying: O Abu Muhammad, I wish to ask you something. He said: Do not ask. I said: If I do not ask you, whom shall I ask? He said: Ask. I said: What do you say about these narrated hadiths, such as: The hearts are between two fingers, and that Allah laughs, or marvels, at one who remembers Him in the markets? He said: Let them pass as they came, without asking how."
